## Script and interface audit

The PowerShell parser reported `AST_ERRORS=0` for
`task-4-regenerate.ps1`; the script itself was not invoked. Its guards are
coherent at the audited HEAD:

- mandatory absolute source/output/Python parameters; exact sibling source
  worktree enforcement; regular-file/directory and reparse-point rejection;
- output root must be new, outside both `five-year-public-pit` and the active
  `canonical-canslim-entry` worktree; archive, normalized, bundle, manifest,
  and audit targets are create-only;
- exact archive manifest fields, byte lengths, ZIP counts/expanded-byte bounds,
  and SHA-256 checks before copy, after copy, and after normalization;
- `Copy-Item` is used for archive staging, so staged archives are copies rather
  than hardlinks; the normalizer sees a complete local archive transaction and
  therefore takes its verified reuse branch before any request session is made;
- preserved provenance/marker hashes are checked, fresh normalized full counts
  are checked, canonical non-XOM rows must remain identical, XOM must be exactly
  `0000034088:reviewed_baseline_cik` with 209 rows split 71 quarterly/30
  annual/108 balance, and FRC must be the sole unresolved-fundamental ticker;
- bundle creation and verification use the unchanged CLI interfaces and record
  the bundle and manifest hashes in a create-only audit JSON.

At current HEAD, `core/sec_pit_fundamentals.py` declares `XOM -> 0000034088`
and applies the reviewed-baseline override after current-ticker/name/chain
resolution. The Task 5 reporting commit `3779b543` changed only
`.superpowers\sdd\2026-08-23-canonical-canslim-entry\progress.md`; the SEC,
bundle-builder, and bundle-verifier interfaces were not changed.

